259
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:37,980
Wait, you wanna cheat? Yep.

260
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:39,677
If one of us becomes king,

261
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:43,357
all the other one has to do is signal
what her number is by blinking, Hmm,

262
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:44,797
which will let us know what Ms.

263
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:46,777
Claire and Prince Dane's numbers are, too.

264
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:51,036
And then, boom, we give them a spicy
order that makes the magic happen.

265
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:53,840
Oh, I guess we could, but...

266
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:56,200
She loves Ms.

267
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:58,760
Claire, so why is she doing this?

268
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:01,260
Okay, I've decided.

269
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:06,020
My order is that number two
and number four must kiss. Ah!

270
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:16,880
You heard me.

271
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:18,864
Numbers two and four must kiss.

272
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:21,617
Now hold on a moment, commoner.

273
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:24,097
I am sure you know that
order is - Absolute.

274
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:26,757
Yeah, that tends to be the
case with the king's orders.

275
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:29,016
I'm not sure what you're waiting for.

276
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:32,720
I see now.

277
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:33,940
I certainly don't.

278
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:37,320
Ray Taylor, you were lying.

279
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:40,660
This game has nothing to
do with being a good king.

280
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:43,940
Were you mocking me?

281
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:50,220
Can't get anything past
you, can we? Pardon?

282
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:53,277
You correctly deduced
that this game has nothing

283
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:55,817
to do with whether you'll
be a great king someday.

284
00:13:55,900 --> 00:14:00,677
As it happens, the true objective was to
see how long it took you to figure it out.

285
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:01,590
Well done.

286
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:03,800
You're saying it was a test.

287
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:06,057
And for that, I humbly
ask for your forgiveness.

288
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:07,800
On the bright side,

289
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:10,197
you refused to comply with
an unreasonable order,

290
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:13,280
and you successfully
identified my true intentions.

291
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:15,477
I'd say you have what it takes.

292
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:18,207
Only a true king could
sort through all that.

293
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:20,900
I'm leaving.

294
00:14:23,660 --> 00:14:24,760
Prince Zane, wait!

295
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:27,972
This won't happen again.

296
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:29,060
Mark my words.

297
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:36,117
Ray, was this whole thing really a test?

298
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,600
Nope, I lied. What?

299
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:38,996
You deceptive snake!

300
00:14:39,220 --> 00:14:40,437
What's wrong with you?

301
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:41,460
Oh, so much.

302
00:14:41,680 --> 00:14:45,327
But hey, at least I managed to
score you some sweet headpacks!

303
00:14:55,680 --> 00:15:00,400
Ray, tell me, am I correct in assuming
that you're what they call gay?

304
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:03,560
Miss Misha,

305
00:15:03,860 --> 00:15:07,477
don't you think that's an awfully
personal question to ask in this setting?

306
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:11,325
It's an awfully personal question
for any setting if you ask me!

307
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:14,087
It doesn't bother me to
talk about it, but...

308
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:15,937
Why do you want to know?

309
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:18,667
Well, you are my best
friend, so I'm curious.

310
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:21,040
Hmm, I mean, I guess?

311
00:15:22,140 --> 00:15:24,258
If it means I like girls, then yeah.

312
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:27,331
I've never been in love with a guy before.

313
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:32,097
Hey, you don't look so
good, what's the matter?

314
00:15:32,180 --> 00:15:33,737
I'm sensing that I am in danger!

315
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:34,650
That's what!

316
00:15:35,020 --> 00:15:35,961
That's not fair.

317
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:39,897
I understand you might be leery of
Rei, given how she often behaves.

318
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:43,297
But Miss Claire, to react that
way just because she's gay?

319
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:46,968
It says more about your ignorance
than it does her character.

320
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:48,790
I'll explain.

321
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:51,797
Let's say, as an example,
that you are straight.

322
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:53,340
I am straight, Misha!

323
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:56,197
And you're madly in love with
Prince Thane, aren't you?

324
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:58,097
You're the one who mad-loved me!

325
00:15:58,180 --> 00:15:59,945
Ray, the jokes aren't helpful.

326
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:02,360
So, tell me, Miss Claire.

327
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:07,100
How would you feel if a man came up to
you and said, Don't molest me? What?

328
00:16:07,260 --> 00:16:09,877
I would never conduct myself
in a lecherous manner!

329
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:10,897
Of course you wouldn't.

330
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:14,200
And yet, you basically
accused Ray of the same thing.

331
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:16,067
You said you were in danger.

332
00:16:17,740 --> 00:16:19,446
Yeah, you're so right, Misha.

333
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:21,449
It doesn't work like that.

334
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:24,937
No one lusts after everyone who
fits their gender preference.

335
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:27,017
It doesn't matter if
you're gay or straight.

336
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:29,335
Attraction is based on the individual.

337
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:31,180
Yes, that's true.

338
00:16:31,340 --> 00:16:32,340
I see your point.

339
00:16:32,740 --> 00:16:36,137
You're saying you fall in love with
the person and not their gender, right?

340
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:39,217
And currently, the one you're in
love with just happens to be a woman.

341
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:40,130
Is that the case?

342
00:16:40,213 --> 00:16:41,860
No, I mean, not exactly.

343
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:44,797
I wouldn't say gender
doesn't matter at all.

344
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,180
Oh, then it does?

345
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:48,150
Yeah.

346
00:16:48,233 --> 00:16:50,297
I get the logic behind
saying gender doesn't

347
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:52,397
matter when you deeply
connect with someone.

348
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:53,598
Like, love is love.

349
00:16:53,940 --> 00:16:58,217
But I can say for sure that I'll never
have those kinds of feelings for a man.

350
00:16:58,300 --> 00:17:01,037
I guess all of this is more
complicated than people think.

351
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:02,997
Some people never have
the chance to learn.

352
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,315
They can't help that.

353
00:17:04,580 --> 00:17:06,517
And I know Miss Clara
doesn't feel the same way.

354
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:08,357
I'm just happy to bask in her presence.

355
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:12,117
But if you ever change your mind and
you want to make out, just let me know.

356
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,030
I never will!

357
00:17:13,220 --> 00:17:15,177
And it's because you
continue to say those things

358
00:17:15,260 --> 00:17:17,837
that I feel like I have to
remain forever on my guard!

359
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:22,000
For the record, I agree with every
part of that last bit. But why?

360
00:17:23,260 --> 00:17:27,080
I really don't ever expect anyone
to reciprocate my feelings.

361
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:29,020
And besides...

362
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:31,600
Go on. What is it?

363
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:34,620
Nothing, never mind.

364
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:37,837
I'm not the only one who's
been unlucky in love.

365
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:39,332
I have to remember that.

366
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:40,916
Finish your thought.

367
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:43,797
Were you about to say you've
given up on Miss Claire?

368
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:46,557
Am I not supposed to respond
to this conversation?

369
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:48,816
Do they realize I'm mere inches away?

370
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:51,784
Actually, I'm a little
confused about that, too.

371
00:17:52,120 --> 00:17:54,237
It's just, from the
way you've been acting,

372
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:56,377
I assumed you were in
love with Miss Claire.

373
00:17:56,460 --> 00:18:00,557
But then you suggested we cheat in that
game to help her get close to Prince Thane.

374
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:01,700
I'm still here!

375
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:04,517
And I believe I heard
something I cannot overlook!

376
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:05,777
I wonder what that could be!

377
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:07,625
I don't think I said anything!

378
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:08,977
Well, I don't know.

379
00:18:09,060 --> 00:18:13,617
I have never thought of it in that way
before, that I would be giving up on her.

380
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:15,237
I've always known she's straight,

381
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:19,597
so it's not as though I expected us
to ride off into the sunset together.

382
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:24,097
Miss Claire has chosen someone she
loves, and I want to support her in that.

383
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:27,600
And besides, I'm honestly
happy just being around her.

384
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:32,820
But most importantly, it was never
about being physical with her.

385
00:18:33,260 --> 00:18:34,720
That isn't my end goal.

386
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,617
All I want is to make her happy.

387
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:40,840
Genuinely happy.

388
00:18:42,260 --> 00:18:43,100
So yeah,

389
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:47,937
if you're questioning whether I can give
up on something that brings me so much joy,

390
00:18:48,020 --> 00:18:51,060
I'm afraid the answer is no.

391
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:53,440
I see.

392
00:18:58,180 --> 00:19:00,651
Anyway, don't worry about me, Miss Claire.

393
00:19:00,860 --> 00:19:03,801
You just keep treating me
the way you always have.

394
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:05,370
Um, all right.

395
00:19:05,820 --> 00:19:09,540
Honestly, I am content with our
relationship exactly as it is.

396
00:19:12,260 --> 00:19:15,200
Beef bowls, extra large servings today.

397
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:16,720
Oh, heck yeah!

398
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:20,677
Talking about all those super complex
subjects made me anxious and hungry.

399
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:22,117
I'm gonna go get a beef bowl!

400
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:23,337
Would you get one for me?

401
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:24,479
I'd like one, too.

402
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:26,465
Beef bowls have been acquired!

403
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:29,597
I brought you one, too,
just in case you're hungry.

404
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:30,510
No, thank you.

405
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:34,717
Everything's definitely as it was before.

406
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:38,077
See nothing's changed at all.

407
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,540
The world of happiness

408
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:41,970
and pain.

409
00:19:42,053 --> 00:19:43,997
I'm used to it.

410
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:47,597
Though almost no one I've loved
has ever returned my feelings.

411
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:51,737
As long as I don't tell them how
I feel they'll remain in my life.

412
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:55,200
But the moment I fall in
love I lose them completely.

413
00:19:58,060 --> 00:19:59,937
Look it's that commoner.

414
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:00,997
Oh right.

415
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:02,957
The one who's been pursuing Miss Claire.

416
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:04,257
Even though they're both girls.

417
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:06,397
Maybe it's my fault.

418
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:09,715
Maybe it's my behavior that's
creating their prejudice.

419
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:12,717
Why do the princes even talk to her.

420
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:15,777
I suppose strange people
make for good entertainment.

421
00:20:15,860 --> 00:20:17,497
That must be it.

422
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:20,777
It's not like anyone could ever
be attracted to a freak like her.

423
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:21,920
I don't mind.

424
00:20:22,420 --> 00:20:26,832
As long as I keep making jokes about
the rejection, I can hold it together.

425
00:20:33,220 --> 00:20:35,980
Oh, I can be awfully clumsy sometimes.

426
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:37,689
Miss Claire, are you okay?

427
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:41,637
I'm sorry, I wasn't paying attention
and my hand must have slipped.

428
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:43,457
You're alright though, aren't you?

429
00:20:43,540 --> 00:20:44,952
You did that on purpose.

430
00:20:45,300 --> 00:20:47,360
I said you're alright, aren't you?

431
00:20:48,140 --> 00:20:49,040
Yes, ma 'am.

432
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:51,790
Commoner!

433
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:52,830
Yes?

434
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:55,297
You've dawdled over your meal long enough.

435
00:20:55,380 --> 00:20:58,968
If you've finished eating, I
have several things to get done.

436
00:21:02,520 --> 00:21:05,873
I never imagined that Miss
Claire would stand up for Ray.

437
00:21:06,160 --> 00:21:09,920
Yes, well, I don't know if I'd
call that standing up for her.

438
00:21:11,420 --> 00:21:12,949
She may not have meant to,

439
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:16,437
but Miss Claire did something
wrong, and she realizes that.

440
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:18,540
It left her feeling unsettled.

441
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:21,430
Fortunately,

442
00:21:21,513 --> 00:21:24,197
though, two girls happen to
come along spouting insults,

443
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:29,045
providing the perfect target on which to
release all of that self-directed anger.

444
00:21:29,340 --> 00:21:31,634
Miss Claire is still very much a child.

445
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:38,237
Avoid the pickled ginger.

446
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:39,849
It is way too sour to eat.

447
00:21:39,940 --> 00:21:41,497
Well, it's supposed to be sour.

448
00:21:41,580 --> 00:21:42,639
That's the appeal.

449
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:45,140
Um, Miss Claire?

450
00:21:47,340 --> 00:21:48,280
What is it?

451
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:50,477
Do you have some sort of problem?

452
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:52,420
Well, not really, no.

453
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:55,130
Um...

454
00:21:55,213 --> 00:21:56,043
I'm just curious.

455
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:58,657
I mean, I want to know
if you still hate me.

456
00:21:58,740 --> 00:21:59,570
You do, right?

457
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:04,360
Of course I still hate you!

458
00:22:12,660 --> 00:22:13,780
Thank you!

459
00:22:14,180 --> 00:22:16,060
And I still love you!

460
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:27,640
Thank you.

461
00:22:51,140 --> 00:22:54,560
I love you.

462
00:23:18,540 --> 00:23:19,370
I'm excited!

463
00:23:19,840 --> 00:23:21,428
I'm so happy, I'm so happy!

464
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:24,537
I'm so happy, and you're so happy!

465
00:23:24,620 --> 00:23:26,897
I'm happy, and I don't want
to know what I'm doing!

466
00:23:26,980 --> 00:23:31,460
I'm so happy, and that's
why I'm so happy! Oh wow!

467
00:23:31,840 --> 00:23:34,899
This world's living in a
world that's going forward!

468
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:36,300
Don't you ask me!

469
00:23:38,620 --> 00:23:40,340
I want to learn my life!

470
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:42,169
I'd like to play with you!

471
00:23:47,460 --> 00:23:50,197
I'm off to go practice my
magic skills for next week.

472
00:23:50,280 --> 00:23:53,737
Oh, are you suggesting that even
a dual caster needs to prepare?

473
00:23:53,820 --> 00:23:56,997
Even with protag specs, I still
can't afford to slack off.

474
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:58,374
Love, effort, victory.

475
00:23:58,680 --> 00:24:00,237
So on the note, give me your love.

476
00:24:00,320 --> 00:24:02,614
I don't know what you're talking about.
